.TH MD_NEW 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_new \- create a streaming mono audio decoder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

morsedec_decoder_t *md_new(const struct morsedec_config *config);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a streaming mono audio decoder.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I config
Configuration to copy, or NULL to use the audio defaults.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns an owned decoder handle on success, or NULL and sets errno on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid configuration, including invalid geometry, band, channel capacity, or
initial WPM.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Storage allocation or FFT planning failed.
.SH REMARKS
Creates an independent decoder and preallocates its FFT, channel slots,
filters, history and decoding state. Release it with md_delete(). The caller
may reuse or discard config after return. Configuration is immutable for the
lifetime of the handle; md_reset() preserves it. See libmorsedec(3) for
validation rules. Accepts mono PCM through md_process() or md_process_s16(),
or calibrated power frames through md_process_spectrum(). The first successful
processing call selects sample or spectrum input until reset.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize this call with all FFTW planner and plan-destruction operations in
the application, including operations for other decoder handles. No such lock
is needed between independent handles during processing.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0 (shared-library ABI
1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_config_init (3),
.BR md_delete (3),
.BR md_new_iq (3),
.BR md_process (3),
.BR md_reset (3)
